WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.320
- I love when people are like,

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.010
Gary V, you're boring.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.419
You say the same shit.

00:00:04.419 --> 00:00:05.710
(everyone laughing)

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.320
And I jump right into and I'm like

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.967
what do you want me to make up shit?

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:11.160
(fast paced music)

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.830
- [Narrator] You got your perspective.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.843
(fast paced music)
(audience applauding)

00:00:15.843 --> 00:00:17.580
I just want to be happy
don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.663
(bouncy piano music)

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.090
- Talk about the content building

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.640
because you talk so much
about having that real content

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.660
behind you versus just something

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.470
that's perceived like the Instagram

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.470
- Well look, I think content
needs to be real to you.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.780
Like, for me entrepreneurial
content comes easy.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.450
I've been selling things since I was six,

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.190
like this was all I've ever been.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.210
Like I don't make content
around education, you know.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.030
So I think where you're going,

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.830
and I wanna make it
contextual for the audience,

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.300
it's like you need to make content

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.860
that is your biggest truth.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.490
The reason I can come here and be like

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.200
I don't need you to read
me, like in backstage,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.480
like I don't need to know the questions

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.620
or I improv talk or when I do like...

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.580
'cause I only talk about my truth.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.410
Like the reason my content
works is 'cause it's my truth.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.890
It's the same reason my wine
content worked a decade ago.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.460
The reason my wine stuff
exploded was 'cause

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.020
I actually tasted wine
and actually told you,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.900
actually what I thought
about it without factoring in

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.270
how it would impact my business.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.920
That was a huge game changer for me.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.490
The day I started wine library TV,

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.930
I thought about it, at like
10 o'clock in the morning

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:28.160
I sent somebody to Best
Buy to buy a camera

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.020
and four hours later,
it was on the internet.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.040
That's how I roll right?

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.450
When I told that kid to go
to Best Buy to buy a camera,

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:38.010
'cause I was gonna record a wine video,

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.720
I completely in my mind at that second,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.161
thought I was going to start QVC.

00:01:43.161 --> 00:01:45.180
(everyone laughing)

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.130
I just want you to know, I just...

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.310
I need you to hear this,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.210
I thought that I would
put out a video everyday

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.090
and I would sell wine in video form.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.370
I had no idea how it would be on video,

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.890
that video if you go look at Episode one

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:57.260
of Wine Library TV is
the first time I ever,

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.550
did something in front of a camera.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.840
My life like, I didn't
know what would happen

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.940
but I knew my intent was, which was QVC.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.770
And then, three hours later,

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.120
after we got it set up and
figured out (mumbling),

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.883
when I filmed it, the
second the light went out,

00:02:12.255 --> 00:02:14.380
this is probably stunningly
one of the most important

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.180
moment of my professional career,

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.840
that I also don't think a whole lot about.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.280
That light went on and I remembered...

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.950
Its amazing how your brain works, right?

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.360
The light goes on and I
remember thinking all of this,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.990
like as I'm saying welcome
to the first episode,

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:29.660
you know how you do
things but another part

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.160
of your brain is doing something else.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:33.087
My other part of my brain saying

00:02:33.087 --> 00:02:35.367
"What if you go to a cocktail party

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:38.267
"and somebody puts a glass
of wine in front of you

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:39.267
"and you taste and they go,

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:40.457
"what do you think?

00:02:40.457 --> 00:02:41.837
"And you say something different

00:02:41.837 --> 00:02:43.607
"than what you said on a video."

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.220
And literally that's
what went through my mind

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.180
and in within the first six minutes

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.440
while I'm setting up what I'm doing there,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:56.340
I switched my thesis from being QVC to,

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.810
I'm just gonna review wine

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.600
and whatever the hell happens happens

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.960
because I don't want to
make myself vulnerable

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.164
to the dateline "ah ha, we caught you."

00:03:04.164 --> 00:03:06.860
(audience laughing)

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.100
And it changed everything.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.930
The reason that show exploded,

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.260
is because there was nobody
on Earth that I was scared of

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.330
not an employee, not my dad,
not my best friend Brandon,

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.520
when I would pan a wine
and we had 80 cases

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.270
of it downstairs and the
whole company would freak,

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.690
there was no confusion that
I was doing the authenticity.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.900
And I think that's why my
content will always work.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.330
Its why I'm willing to say things

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.840
like I said earlier that
I'm not gonna pander

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.970
to the current state of what's accepted.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:34.280
If I just shoot my truth 24/7

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.300
and I believe that for you too.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.930
Everybody thinks and
overthinks their content,

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.110
'cause you're trying to
figure out what will work

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.620
versus realizing your individual truth

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.773
of the moment is what will work.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.300
The reason my sister who now has decided

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:53.040
to not be a stay at home mom
and get into real estate,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.420
the reason she's getting
some attraction on Instagram,

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.890
she's just talking about failures,

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:59.179
because she's failing, which is so shit.

00:03:59.179 --> 00:04:01.820
(everyone laughing)

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.130
But that doesn't come natural,

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.890
that doesn't seem like the
thing you're trying to do.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.820
How do you instill
confidence to get somebody

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:09.943
to list your home with them,
if you're saying you suck?

00:04:09.943 --> 00:04:11.430
(audience laughing)

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.330
Because that works better than faking it.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.380
- She's honest, she's honest about it.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:18.190
- Everybody here can put
out a ton of content,

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.300
nobody is because everybody
is overthinking it,

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.980
because they're pandering
it to what works and likes

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.390
or will it get shared
or who cares about me.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.910
It's all insecurities and defense.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.550
If you literally made a video everyday

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:33.410
on Instagram for one minute,
that you just recapped

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.180
what happened that day in a minute,

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.303
on a selfie video, you'll do well.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.970
That's why reality TV does well.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.500
That's why social does well.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.980
People want truths, your biggest strength

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:48.213
is that you are individual humans.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.280
Everybody is just full of shit.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.350
How many people's self esteem
is completely wrapped up

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.903
into how many likes they
get on a post on Instagram?

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.403
That's some dangerous shit.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.540
So that's what they're looking for.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.290
'Cause they're right, you'll
get more likes (shruging).

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.870
You know.
(sneering)

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.040
And look, I mean I think
it's super fast, I mean,

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.430
people that overshare their families

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.250
over it index all the time.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.110
We like that shit.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.620
We like the babies and the
dating and the divorce.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.460
Look at our behaviors of what we consume.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.210
And that's great and for
people that are comfortable

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.650
with that and that's their truth,

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.650
I'm pumped, like if my kids
decide to go that route,

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:25.627
I'm not gonna judge them and be like,

00:05:25.627 --> 00:05:29.210
"no no, it's do you but do you"

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.420
like never waver from that

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.490
'cause the second you start
wavering, it doesn't feel good.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.810
Just gonna wake up and be
like why did I do that?

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.517
You know, so I would stick to what it is.

